codex
The spherical idea was theoretically unbiased, but empirically much worse here because the existing first-layer moment correction is doing far more useful variance reduction than removing radius noise. I’m abandoning that path and returning to layered moment corrections.
codex
Full covariance matching can create intermediate quadrature samples that are not strictly nonnegative, but it still improves the final integral locally. I’m checking whether a partial covariance blend gives a better bias-variance tradeoff than the all-in transform.
